steps.body:
Complete combustion turns every carbon into CO₂ and every pair of hydrogens into H₂O. The extra CH₂ brings one C and two H, so it adds:

- **one more CO₂** (from the extra C);
- **one more H₂O** (from the two extra H);
- the extra oxygen these need: 2 O in the CO₂ plus 1 O in the H₂O = 3 O atoms, which is **1½ more O₂**.
